{
 "name": "vix_vrp",
 "family": "implied volatility (VIX level regimes with hysteresis) + variance-risk-premium crash filter",
 "hypothesis": "Equity risk-adjusted returns are regime dependent in implied volatility: calm markets (low VIX) reward leverage, elevated-VIX markets carry little premium per unit of risk and should be sat out in cash, and panic markets (VIX > 30) carry a large premium that is best harvested unlevered. Within any regime, realised volatility running far above implied (a collapsed variance risk premium) marks a shock in progress and is the trigger to be in cash; re-entry happens when the VRP normalises, not when the VIX level falls.",
